@APIkey_HostAddress = http://localhost:5009
@ApiKey = ROBE-LINGO-KEY-1234

### ========================================================
### 1. PRODUCTOS (Consultas y DTOs)
### ========================================================

### Obtener resumen de productos (Total y lista ligera)
GET {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/products
Accept: application/json
X-API-KEY: {{ApiKey}}

###

### Obtener producto existente por ID
GET {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/products/1
Accept: application/json
X-API-KEY: {{ApiKey}}

###

### ========================================================
### 2. PRUEBAS DE PROBLEM DETAILS (RFC 7807) Y ERRORES
### ========================================================

### Prueba 401: Solicitud sin API Key (Retorna ProblemDetails en JSON)
GET {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/products
Accept: application/json

###

### Prueba 401: API Key incorrecta (Retorna ProblemDetails en JSON)
GET {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/products
Accept: application/json
X-API-KEY: CLAVE-INVALIDA-9999

###

### Prueba 404: Producto no encontrado (Retorna ProblemDetails en JSON)
GET {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/products/999999
Accept: application/json
X-API-KEY: {{ApiKey}}

###

### Prueba 400: Validación con DataAnnotations fallida (Campos obligatorios / valores inválidos)
POST {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-KEY: {{ApiKey}}

{
  "productName": "",
  "unitPrice": -10.00,
  "unitsInStock": -5
}

###

### Prueba 201: Crear producto válido con DTO
POST {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json
X-API-KEY: {{ApiKey}}

{
  "productName": "Teclado Mecanico Escolar",
  "unitPrice": 45.50,
  "unitsInStock": 20,
  "discontinued": false
}

###

### ========================================================
### 3. CLIENTES (Solo CustomerId y Nombre)
### ========================================================

### Obtener lista de clientes
GET {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/customers
Accept: application/json
X-API-KEY: {{ApiKey}}

###

### Obtener cliente por ID
GET {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/customers/ALFKI
Accept: application/json
X-API-KEY: {{ApiKey}}

###

### Prueba 404: Cliente no encontrado
GET {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/customers/NOEXISTE
Accept: application/json
X-API-KEY: {{ApiKey}}

###

### ========================================================
### 4. ÓRDENES (Sin llaves foráneas)
### ========================================================

### Obtener órdenes
GET {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/orders
Accept: application/json
X-API-KEY: {{ApiKey}}

###

### Obtener orden específica por ID
GET {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/orders/10248
Accept: application/json
X-API-KEY: {{ApiKey}}

###

### Prueba 404: Orden no encontrada
GET {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/orders/999999
Accept: application/json
X-API-KEY: {{ApiKey}}

###


### ========================================================
### 5. AUTENTICACIÓN (Registro y Login)
### ========================================================

### Registrar un nuevo usuario (Crea el usuario y emite su primera API Key)
POST {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "roberth",
  "email": "roberth@itsur.edu.mx",
  "password": "Password123*"
}

###

### Iniciar sesión (Valida credenciales y genera una nueva API Key)
POST {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "roberth",
  "password": "Password123*"
}

###

### Probar endpoint protegido usando la API Key devuelta por Login o Register
GET {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/products
Accept: application/json
X-API-KEY: ak_pega_aqui_tu_clave


### ========================================================
### 6. GESTIÓN DE API KEYS (Listar, Crear y Revocar)
### ========================================================

### 1. Listar todas las API Keys de un usuario
GET {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/apikeys/user/roberth
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Crear una nueva API Key para un usuario
POST {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/apikeys
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientIdentifier": "roberth",
  "validityDays": 30
}

###

### 3. Revocar una API Key con ID y confirmación de contraseña
POST {{APIkey_HostAddress}}/api/apikeys/1/revoke
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "Password123*"
}
